-- title:
--   Supersingular residue discs from an affine chart, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$, a nonzero $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$; let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)(M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$), let $s\in W$, and let $\mathrm{hle}$ witness that the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field sits inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Further data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, the contraction $A_b$ of $A$ to $K_b$, assumed a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\varpi_b$. Then, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'/k_0$, every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ which is an $A_b$-algebra, contains the image of the Laurent expansion $j$ and is stable under all automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ ($\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$), every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residue field $\mathrm{FSS}$ such that $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every element of $\mathrm{FSS}$ is a ratio of residues of elements of $B$, every finite set $N$ of places $Q$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ characterised by: $Q\notin N$ iff all residues of elements of $B$ lie in $Q$'s valuation subring, and assumed stable under the residual automorphisms $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms and preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every system of subrings $S_Q\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with ring maps $\varphi_Q:A_b[X]\to S_Q$ and $\chi_Q:S_Q\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ satisfying, for each $Q\notin N$, the package of conditions summarised here — $\varphi_Q$ extends the inclusion of $A_b$, $\chi_Q\circ\varphi_Q$ is the residue map of $A$ on constants and kills $X$, $S_Q$ is local with $\ker\chi_Q$ its maximal ideal, $S_Q$ generates the compositum of $k_0(K_b)$ and $F_0$ as a fraction field, $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type, $S_Q\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ with membership in the maximal ideal detected by divisibility by $\varphi_Q(\varpi_b)$, the residues of $S_Q$ are $Q$-integral and reduce to $\chi_Q$, $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ equals $1$, and $S_Q$ is the localisation $\{g/h: g,h\in B,\ \bar h(Q)\neq 0\}$ of $B$ — and with the discs $D_Q$ defined by: a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $D_Q$ iff $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_Q$ is $P$-integral with $P$-value in $A$, and that value has $A$-valuation $<1$ exactly when $\chi_Q f=0$: the conclusion is that (i) for $Q,Q'\notin N$, a common member $P\in D_Q\cap D_{Q'}$ forces $Q=Q'$; (ii) for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$, $\mathrm{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$; and (iii) for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every $Q$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q\in N$ iff $Q\in N$ (as already assumed of $N$), and for $Q\notin N$ the translated disc $\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D_Q\}$ equals $D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ instance of the statement that the residue discs cut out on the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-function field by the smooth points of an affine chart of a semistable model are pairwise disjoint, avoid the cusps (the $j$-function has non-negative order on them), and are permuted compatibly with the action of the level automorphisms on the ends. It is used in the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings and of the stalks at the smooth points of the base of the chart.
-- source:
